# THE HERO IMAGE IS A PLACEHOLDER. Two other candidates are in play and the
# choice is not made, so swapping it is these four lines and nothing else.
#
# ONE FILENAME, DELIBERATELY. `preloadImage` is what base.njk preloads AND
# what the <img> takes as its src, so the two cannot drift apart. A preload
# pointing at a file the page does not use is a wasted download and a missed
# LCP, and it is the failure that happens when a swap edits one and not the
# other.
#
# The dimensions are the file's true intrinsic size and MUST be re-read from
# the replacement. The frame sets no height, so this pair is what reserves the
# space, and a stale pair reintroduces layout shift on the page's LCP element.
preloadImage: cs-img-leaves-landscape.webp
heroWidth: 1400
heroHeight: 784
heroAlt: Leaves ranged in a row, one subject studied specimen by specimen
---
